# Repo-wide secrets. Copy to .env, fill in, keep local — .env is git-ignored.
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env

# GitHub fine-grained PAT for the codespaces tool. Only the account permission
# "Plan" (read) is needed (billing usage of your user) — no repository access,
# no organization involvement.
#   1. github.com -> Settings -> Developer settings ->
#      Personal access tokens -> Fine-grained tokens -> Generate new token
#   2. Token name: e.g. "utils.d codespaces dashboard"
#   3. Expiration: set one (e.g. 90 days)
#   4. Resource owner: your personal account
#   5. Repository access: "Public Repositories (read-only)" (select no repositories)
#   6. Account permissions: Plan -> Read-only
#   7. Generate token, paste it below.
GITHUB_TOKEN=